/**
 * LIGHTNING WEB COMPONENTS (LWC)
 */

// Component Architecture

RULE = Create small, reusable components with single responsibilities
RULE = Use out-of-the-box LWC elements until the feature cannot be built using standard components
RULE = Always use some space above the component to display global error messages
RULE = Use standard pagination for large data sets if available
RULE = For dynamic expressions in HTML file never use double quotes(Wrong = "{contact.Id}" AND "{handleButtonClick}", Right = {contact.Id} AND {handleButtonClick})

// Data Handling

RULE = Use the @wire decorator to efficiently retrieve data, preferring Lightning Data Service.
RULE = Only use @track decorator for objects and arrays that need deep reactivity tracking.
RULE = Remember that primitive properties are reactive by default since Spring '20 release.
RULE = For object/array mutations, either use @track or implement immutable update patterns.
RULE = Implement error handling and display user-friendly error messages.
RULE = Utilize SLDS (Salesforce Lightning Design System) for consistent styling and layout.

// Performance

RULE = Avoid direct DOM manipulation
RULE = Use conditional rendering with the lwc:if directive
RULE = Prefer client-side filtering over server calls when appropriate
RULE = Lazy load components when appropriate
RULE = Use CSS instead of JavaScript for animations when possible

// Styling

RULE = Follow SLDS design patterns and guidelines
RULE = Use SLDS utility classes instead of custom CSS when possible
RULE = Encapsulate component-specific styles with :host selector
RULE = Use CSS variables for theming and customization
RULE = Implement responsive design patterns
RULE = Use mobile and desktop for responsive design
RULE = Test styling across all supported devices and screen sizes